{#
  Generated-data marker — shared CSS for the `**value**` convention
  (docs/DATA_INTEGRITY.md #4.1a, decided by Zach 2026-07-23).

  Any fake/generated/inferred/sample value that is shown must be visually
  flagged. `.generated` is that flag: real data around it stays plain,
  the wrapped span reads as "not confirmed" at a glance (dashed outline +
  accent color + a small superscript marker, not just bold — bold alone
  is too easy to mistake for ordinary emphasis).
#}
<style>
.generated{
  position:relative;
  color:var(--accent);
  border-bottom:1px dashed var(--accent);
  cursor:help;
}
.generated::after{
  content:"generated";
  position:absolute; left:50%; bottom:100%; transform:translateX(-50%);
  margin-bottom:6px;
  font-size:10px; letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase;
  font-weight:700; font-family:var(--font-body);
  color:var(--bg); background:var(--accent);
  padding:3px 7px; border-radius:5px; white-space:nowrap;
  opacity:0; pointer-events:none; transition:opacity .12s;
}
.generated:hover::after, .generated:focus-visible::after{opacity:1;}
</style>
